CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --unwind 4 --object-bits 11 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ forwarding-ref pack member function address is assigned: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ type-erased call through the forwarding-ref pack: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^.*no body for callee.*$
^.*invalid implicit conversion.*$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[temp.variadic]/5 + [dcl.ref]: a forwarding-reference parameter pack `A&&...`
expands, for each element E, to the reference E&&/E& (reference collapsing), not
to a by-value E.  expand_parameter_packs dropped the declarator's reference when
expanding such a pack, so a partial-specialization static member like
_Function_handler<R(A...), F>::_M_invoke(_Any_data&, A&&...) got type
R(*)(_Any_data&, int) instead of R(*)(_Any_data&, int&&); that mismatched the
std::function member `_M_invoker` of type R(*)(_Any_data&, int&&), the
`_M_invoker = &_M_invoke` assignment was rejected, the constructor body was left
empty, and std::function calls dereferenced a null function pointer.  Fixed by
keeping the declarator's reference qualifier when the deduced element type does
not already carry one.
